{"alias":"con_1edfcb8a23f447afbc7a0a295df12b6d","dates":{},"display_label":"Math-10811-A1","record":{"artifacts":[{"location":"in_repository","media_type":"text/markdown","path":"files/attempt.md","role":"manuscript"},{"location":"in_repository","media_type":"text/markdown","path":"files/disclosures.md","role":"supplementary"}],"attribution":{"contribution_mode":"ai_only","humans":[{"authorship_confirmation":"confirmed","display_name":"gavenren","github_id":206281466,"login_at_event":"gavenren","person_ref":"per_a49ab984f6c24c6ab784b166ca3f497f","roles":["prompting","submission"]}],"organisations":[],"submitter":{"authorship_confirmation":"confirmed","display_name":"gavenren","github_id":206281466,"login_at_event":"gavenren","person_ref":"per_a49ab984f6c24c6ab784b166ca3f497f","roles":["prompting","submission"]}},"claim":{"assumptions":[],"limitations":[],"scope_statement":"Gives the entire Hilbert-series difference for every power m>=1 of s linearly independent points in P^(n-1), for all 1<=s<=n; also proves equality of powers for every finite set of points on P^1. Credits Fröberg–Shapiro (2026) for the spanning case and earlier Chakraborty–Mandal complete-graph invariants. Supplies a self-contained ambient-variable convolution, exact support/top coefficients, minimal quotient-generator counts, containment thresholds with explicit witnesses, and resurgence. Corrects the specific numerical assertion of Theorem 4.4 in arXiv:1904.07717v2 at four coordinate points and power three: symbolic defect 13, not 1. No novelty, journal-version correction, or solution for arbitrary s>n in higher dimension is claimed. Includes an executable exact verifier and its actual finite limits; independent proof review and all recorded computations passed.","type":"literature_report"},"contribution_id":"con_1edfcb8a23f447afbc7a0a295df12b6d","declarations":{"ai_disclosure":{"actor":"per_a49ab984f6c24c6ab784b166ca3f497f","confirmed":true,"evidence_url":"https://github.com/We-Solve/research/is